Andrew Kerr <andykerr@SPAMGUARD.blueyonder.co.uk> writes:
> It would appear certain monster types are not affected by extinction 
> (or genocide?) on the Quest levels. In particular, those guaranteed to 
> be generated on some levels - for the Knight quest that includes 
> quasits and ochre jellies. I've not found the code that deals with 
> Quest monster generation. Would this be considered a bug? I can imagine 
> the DevTeam not wanting Quest nasties to be genocided, but why not 
> rendered extinct?

The generation of specific Quest enemies contributes to extinction,
but is not restricted by it. If anything's a bug, it's the former, not
the latter; extinction is supposed to represent the depletion of the
population of the Mazes of Menace, and the Quest is theoretically set
elsewhere. (Ideally it'd have its own extinction counter, but that
could get tricky.)

